<title>JAPAN: Japan exporters sag on strengthening yen.</title>
<headline>Japan exporters sag on strengthening yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Japanese exporters sagged in the Tuesday afternoon session, discouraged by the strengthening of the yen against the dollar, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0502 GMT, Sony Corp was down 90 yen at 9,710, while NEC Corp had fallen 10 yen to 1,590.</p>
<p>Toyota Motor Corp had lost 20 to stand at 3,630 yen, Pioneer Electronic Corp was down 50 yen at 2,600 and Canon Inc had shed 30 to stand at 2,850.  </p>
<p>&quot;After the yen pushed past 114 yen to the dollar, exporters became weak. But the selling is not very heavy and the share prices have been spared sharp losses,&quot; a trader at a second-tier brokerage said.</p>
</text>
